{"id": "EUVD-2026-59377", "enisaUuid": "07f914d0-b990-36bf-82d2-7a247c6d9437", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfs/ntfs3: add bounds check to run_get_highest_vcn()\n\nrun_get_highest_vcn() parses a packed NTFS mapping-pairs buffer without\nany length bound, relying solely on a 0x00 terminator to stop.  A\ncrafted $LogFile UpdateMappingPairs record whose embedded attribute\ncontains mapping-pairs runs without a terminator causes the function to\nread past the slab allocation, triggering a KASAN slab-out-of-bounds\nread on mount.\n\nThe sibling function run_unpack() received an analogous bounds-check in\ncommit b62567bca474 (\"ntfs3: add buffer boundary checks to run_unpack()\"),\nbut run_get_highest_vcn() was missed.\n\nTake a run_buf_size parameter and reject any run header whose payload\nwould extend past the buffer end, mirroring the pattern used by\nrun_unpack().  The caller in fslog.c passes the remaining attribute\nbytes after the mapping-pairs offset.\n\nKASAN report (on mainline v7.1 merge window HEAD):\n\n  BUG: KASAN: slab-out-of-bounds in run_get_highest_vcn+0x3c0/0x410\n  Read of size 1 at addr ffff88800e2d5400 by task mount/72\n  Call Trace:\n   run_get_highest_vcn+0x3c0/0x410\n   do_action.isra.0+0x3ba8/0x7b50\n   log_replay+0x9ddd/0x10200\n   ntfs_loadlog_and_replay+0x4ad/0x610\n   ntfs_fill_super+0x214a/0x4540", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:57:17", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T18:55:26", "baseScore": 8.4, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c69b9003332917b652175d5fa9d84158c5ed8617", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8afc24a884aff6a6f08028bd779ee65c40054455", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c23083b472a720c3f60b147db05b25b751c7c1bf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a31893206588374d7d16fad387189d8165c7efd3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/41081202eb823f5b27ff164b12010b24428100ad", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bb11485a87fbb2254b62cfed630b699d50e57da8"], "aliases": ["GHSA-pcrg-m6wx-53ch", "CVE-2026-72478"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "00561595-f16e-35a0-b186-13c1f50cb7bc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "075a877b-176b-3657-868c-90974cc8a419", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bf7ac4a1d3bfc6e56e54635c3d331a68170d37c9 <8afc24a884aff6a6f08028bd779ee65c40054455"}, {"id": "111aac45-b4d2-3d0d-9b47-c2808039a50b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7.0.4 <7.1"}, {"id": "2c4e8e39-b879-3ed0-8a6e-95aeb3c65f63", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.1.175 <6.1.178"}, {"id": "3ceea0d4-076d-36c8-b916-81c73c5654a8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.178"}, {"id": "4b132fe0-3dcf-318b-8496-a234d7aea46d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "55ef952e-ce2b-3d45-8362-800751b5a6a3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b62567bca47408e6739dee75f02a2113548af875 <41081202eb823f5b27ff164b12010b24428100ad"}, {"id": "56274ea2-7a99-3370-bf79-cc9583ea436a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.18.27 <6.18.40"}, {"id": "600d6e7b-5c00-332d-a360-0a0642e2f2d1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.40"}, {"id": "7217696d-f267-316d-b274-1626f48c50d4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d3012690a7065d9ca86521a525ad11e8af491d45 <a31893206588374d7d16fad387189d8165c7efd3"}, {"id": "75b770d3-2d2f-3c17-aa75-87ac40d6b257", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "41aadf5cb482793a24e05aa136224e179a778586"}, {"id": "891d0daf-aba2-